  "summary": "I am a graphic designer who graduated from Rutgers University in 2020, where I developed a strong foundation in visual communication. During that time, I created logos, posters, book jackets, wireframes, and digital layouts for websites and magazines, and I even had the opportunity to exhibit my artwork in a Rutgers University gallery.\n\nAlthough my career path later led me into full-stack web development through Revature—where I quickly learned core Java, SQL, AWS databases, servlets, HTTP APIs, SOAP, JavaScript, CSS, HTML, XML, JavaBeans, Hibernate, Spring, Spring MVC, AWS S3, Spring Boot, Angular, microservices, DevOps, Jenkins, and Docker—I’ve realized that my true passion remains in design.\n\nNow, with both creative and technical experience, I’m excited to return to my roots as a graphic designer, bringing a richer, more versatile skill set to the work I create.",
